{
  "rationale": "The plant automaton G1 models the robot's combined perception and motion execution, including all possible sensor outcomes and motion commands. The specification automata E1-E4 enforce safe, progress-oriented exploration: E1 binds clear perception to forward/random_walk actions, E2-E3 enforce conservative obstacle recovery (directed turns or backward only for front obstacles), and E4 prevents repeated backward actions and ensures quick return to exploration after recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Model both perception and motion as a single plant automaton for determinism and to capture open-loop action semantics.",
    "Use separate specifications to enforce safe recovery, forward bias, and to prevent chaining of recovery actions, ensuring steady progress and reliable collision avoidance."
  ],
